The two copies of $u$ and of $B_{\rm base}$ pay for distinct finite
approximation and coefficient-realization errors. Quadrature errors
are already contained in the oriented integral endpoints. The ancillary
fields \texttt{scalar\_bounds} contain the resulting exact sums and
strict surpluses.
